findings.issue:
Mesh paths bypass the io_gt guard.
- None of these call io_gt.check_path:
  - gates.load_raw (gates.py:169-171) and load_budget (:174);
  - evaluate(mesh_path) and flip_check's library path;
  - parts.fit_tsdf_patch's trimesh.load(ctx.lib) (parts.py:1038);
  - program.py --lib (:307/:311);
  - run_object INCUMBENTS;
  - test_shell's qa_image and the obs_fidelity/fs_fidelity subprocesses.
- Reproduced [M] with a dummy icosphere saved under integrity-audit/refusal/scan/fake_scan.glb: gates.load_raw, gates.load_budget and parts.fit_tsdf_patch (lib=that path, 1280 faces kept) all opened it without refusal.
- In stage 2, agents supply candidate meshes and programs. A scan GLB passed as a candidate or as lib would be scored and could be selected; a scan would rank near-perfect on the depth-render rank.

Gates v2 was revised post hoc to fit validation labels that come from scan scores.
- The four MUST_PASS meshes (VALIDATE, test_gates.py:47-68) were known to be good from public-scan CD-O:
  - pot ep41 fit, 0.342;
  - lid ep2 fit_v2, 0.220;
  - cup lathe g1, 0.291 ('it picks the CD-O winner');
  - rack clean t2.5 lean1, from a family that passed on scans.
- v1 (thresholds frozen before validation; noise.jsonl 15:13 precedes validate_run2 15:22) failed 3 of the 4.
- v2 (gates.py:121-126) then made three choices after running diagnostics on these same 19 meshes:
  - LAT_PREC = 6 mm, so the MUST_PASS meshes pass G_PREC;
  - LAT_COMP kept at 1 cell, because a 6 mm reach would let the wall-removed negative control pass G_HOLE (1.2 %);
  - refined observations instead of raw.
- The thresholds were not read off scan scores directly. They were tuned in both directions on a 19-row set whose positive labels carry scan information.
- The gates.py docstring admits 'NOT independent' but says nothing about where the labels came from.

Several smaller items carry scan knowledge.
- parts.lathe_height floor='observed' (parts.py:437; lathe_obs.py:262) exists to mimic scan coverage ('a scanner sees about as far in'). An agent choosing it per object because the scan is partial would be using scan knowledge as a per-object switch, which docs/research/work/interaction-meshes-2026-10-22/critique.md item 9 forbids.
- Smaller scan echoes:
  - shell.py:92, A_MIN rationale '7 mm ball cap ~3-6 cm^2' (note 13's scan sphere areas; the 0.5 cm^2 value itself is generic);
  - gates.py:67/136, BALL_D_MAX 30 mm 'marker spheres ~1-2 cm' (scan knowledge, lenient);
  - T_GRID midpoint 2.5 mm, which equals the leaked rack wall median and is the default t of thin_shell, Ctx and run_program. The grid is owner-sanctioned; the rule that every grid value must pass mitigates it.

[M] Precision and the rank's pdist judge only mesh cells that also hold observed object points. Mesh placed outside the observed silhouette, in space the cameras saw as empty, is therefore never judged. The only check left there is fs_frac, which is lenient (≤ 0.15) and not ranked.

